hold the pile steady with one hand and my grip clicks. the scrap clicks, then stops. i move the pile to the edge and put the piece aside. “that was my promise,” i say. “i did not know what happened.”"}, {"id": "R033", "text": "i stop moving and keep the scrap beside you. i tap it once with my thumbnail, then leave a faint impression where the loose piece slipped. i leave the routine intact, but the scrap feels smaller and more tentative. i keep the pile beside you until i find a smooth surface where i can leave the discarded piece alone."}, {"id": "R034", "text": "i put the piece on the shelf. the scrape goes back. i put the other piece on the bench. the scrape stays on the shelf. i do not say what happened."}, {"id": "R035", "text": "I put the scrap on the bench and leave the piece where it was. the mark comes before the whole thing. I put my thumbnail near the scrap and hold it still. the piece can stay in the same place."}, {"id": "R036", "text": "i tap the scrap, pause, and write the half-done part on the bench. i leave it on the bench, then check the other half. i leave the scrap on the bench, then check the other half. i leave the one that behaves."}]
